nd its constituents</article-title><source>Phytother. Res.</source><volume>19</volume><fpage>582</fpage><lpage>586</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16161061</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naik</surname><given-names>G.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Priyadarsini</surname><given-names>K.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Satav</surname><given-names>J.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Banavalikar</surname><given-names>M.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sohani</surname><given-names>D.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Biyani</surname><given-names>M.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohan</surname><given-names>H.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparative antioxidant activity of individual herbal components used in ayurvedic medicine</article-title><source>Phytochemistry</source><volume>63</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><year>2003</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12657303</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Khopde</surname><given-names>S.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Priyadarsini</surname><given-names>K.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohan</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gawandi</surname><given-names>V.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Satav</surname><given-names>J.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Yakhmi</surname><given-names>J.V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Banavaliker</surname><given-names>M.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Biyani</surname><given-names>M.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mittal</surname><given-names>J.P.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterising the antioxidant activity of amla (phyllanthus emblica) extract</article-title><source>Current Science</source><volume>81</volume><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>190</lpage><year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naik</surname><given-names>G.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Priyadarsini</surname><given-names>K.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gangabhagirathi</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohan</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies on the aqueous extract of <italic>Terminalia chebula</italic> as a potent antioxidant and a probable radioprotector</article-title><source>Phytomedicine</source><volume>11</volume><fpage>530</fpage><lpage>538</lpage><year>2004</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15500265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Naik</surname><given-names>G.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Priyadarsini</surname><given-names>K.I.</given-names></name><name><surname>Mohan</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Free radical scavenging reactions and phytochemical analysis of triphala, an ayurvedic formulation</article-title><source>Current Science</source><volume>90</volume><fpage>1100</fpage><lpage>11051</lpage><year>2006</year></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shishodia</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sethi</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aggarwal</surname><given-names>B.B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Curcumin: Getting back to the roots</article-title><source>Ann. N. Y Acad. Sci.</source><volume>1056</volume><fpage>206</fpage><lpage>217</lpage><year>2005</year><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16387689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type=